        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a **city-wide arcane lockdown**, but the catch is it could **isolate parts of the city and endanger or restrict anyone not protected by council-approved amulets**.\n\nBased on CANON and OBSERVED facts, the proposal tied to the emergency is the **\u201cProposed arcane lockdown\u201d** (the city, defenses). This aligns with the council actively choosing a plan to handle the crisis and threats spreading through the city (City Council governance, City operational_status).\n\nThe catch comes from how that lockdown interacts with existing systems:\n- The city could be **\u201cat risk of having parts isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed\u201d** (OBSERVED).\n- The chamber and broader defenses rely on **amulets that mark individuals as friendly**, meaning others may be treated as threats or blocked by defenses (CANON: City Council defenses; Players defenses).\n- Given concerns about **defense integrity**, the lockdown may not be perfectly controlled (CANON).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Proposed arcane lockdown; amulet-based identification system\n- Operational Status: City threatened; possible isolation of districts\n- Governance: Council vote determines adoption; multiple competing plans\n- Geography: Hidden passages and tunnels increase risk of uneven lockdown effects",
      "embedding_similarity": null,
