      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherds are a cult known as the Shepherd\u2019s Flock, and they answer to the power/entity Maelthor.\n\nThe \u201cShepherds\u201d refer to the **Shepherd\u2019s Flock**, a cult group actively operating in the city (notably staging protests and recruiting). They present themselves publicly as defenders of human settlements, but internally they justify extreme actions as necessary \u201ccleansing.\u201d\n\n- **CANON/OBSERVED**: They recruit individuals\u2014especially those transformed or affected\u2014into their ranks and indoctrinate them into their mission.\n- **CANON**: Their ideology centers on purification and **ensuring human supremacy**, framing violence or corruption as righteous acts.\n- **OBSERVED**: They are explicitly identified as **followers of Maelthor**.\n- **OBSERVED**: Their alignment is tied to **Maelthor\u2019s influence and emergence**, suggesting an active, possibly growing power behind them.\n\nThere\u2019s no conflicting attribution: all relevant facts consistently point to **Maelthor** as the power they serve.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Faction: Followers of Maelthor (OBSERVED)\n- Role: Cultists staging protests and recruiting (CANON/OBSERVED)\n- Goals: \u201cCleanse\u201d the world, ensure human supremacy, recruit the transformed (CANON)\n- Alignment: Devoted to Maelthor\u2019s influence and emergence (OBSERVED)\n- Activity: Active recruitment and public agitation at city gates (CANON/OBSERVED)",
