      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards, and he views the cult as a dangerous misuse of magic\u2014pushing for aggressive arcane detection and containment measures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright represents the Wizard\u2019s College on the council (OBSERVED role/governance). He is a gnome headmaster and the primary arcane authority in discussions.\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly anti\u2013dark magic. He sees the corrupted meat as a \u201cperversion of magic\u201d (CANON loyalty/alignment) and takes the threat very seriously. As a result, he advocates for a proactive, magic-heavy response: deploying Wizard\u2019s College resources, using detection spells, and even planning a magical lockdown of the city (OBSERVED goals). He is also prepared to present his plan first and can be persuaded to share or combine magical solutions.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Headmaster of the Wizard\u2019s College; council representative for arcane interests\n- Goals: Magical lockdown, detection runes, deploy arcane resources against the cult\n- Attitude toward cult: Sees it as a dangerous corruption of magic that must be countered decisively\n- Personality: Brilliant, inventive, but somewhat distractible (CANON mental_state/portrayal)",
