      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight **dead**\u2014specifically \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThe projection shows conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**: he both \u201cescapes\u201d while invisible toward a secret tunnel and is later \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d Because decapitation is a terminal outcome, it overrides earlier escape attempts. The most current state is therefore that he is dead.\n\nSupporting sequence:\n- OBSERVED: The Wolf drinks an invisibility potion and attempts escape via a secret passage.\n- OBSERVED: Bonogo pursues and attacks him.\n- OBSERVED (terminal): \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d\n- OBSERVED: Bonogo\u2019s role includes \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d\n\nSo even though he briefly fled/invisible, the fight ultimately resolves with his death, and his body is no longer intact.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d (final)\n- Prior state: Invisible, attempting escape via secret tunnel\n- Faction: cultist\n- Role: central adversary in council chamber battle\n- Mental state: desperate, begging to be killed (pre-death)",
