      "answer": "TL;DR: The projection does not state that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior is linked to The Wolf\u2019s influence, which appears to be something different or at least unconfirmed.\n\nFrom the available facts, **Guards** have explicit markers of corruption: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED), along with mutations and interaction with corrupted meat. That establishes a clear, identifiable corruption state.\n\nFor **Thalia**, there is no such physical or mechanical indicator. The only relevant fact is that **\u201cThe Wolf orders Thalia to attack the group\u201d** (OBSERVED, Entity: the Wolf, goals). Additionally, The Wolf himself has \u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d (OBSERVED), tying him more directly to the same corruption pattern as the guards.\n\nBecause Thalia lacks any stated corruption markers (like the oily sheen) and is acting under The Wolf\u2019s direction, the safest grounded conclusion is:\n- Not confirmed corrupted like the guards\n- Likely influenced, controlled, deceived, or acting under orders instead\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards (OBSERVED): oily sheen in eyes \u2192 confirmed corruption\n- The Wolf (OBSERVED): oily sheen in eyes; issues commands\n- Thalia (OBSERVED via Wolf): ordered to attack; no corruption markers given",
