      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room actively interferes with arcane traps (force bursts + paralysis), illusion effects that disorient, environmental hazards like falling debris, and alarm systems that escalate the fight\u2014while selectively ignoring amulet-wearers.\n\nThe chamber itself is hostile terrain:\n\n- **Arcane trap bursts** (CANON/OBSERVED): These can hit players for **2d6 force damage** and **temporarily paralyze** them. Per CANON, **players without amulets are targeted**, while **Guards are exempt** due to their amulets.\n- **Illusion effects** (CANON): The party is already **disoriented by illusory walls/illusion spells**, and duplicates (like the Wolf\u2019s) have precedent for confusion. Expect movement and positioning to get scrambled.\n- **Environmental hazards** (OBSERVED): The room can **force players to dodge falling debris**, adding pressure and breaking formation.\n- **Rune alarms & escalation** (OBSERVED): **Rune alarms alert guards**, bringing reinforcements or tightening control mid-fight.\n- **Ambient feedback** (CANON): The **wall\u2019s constant hum changes** when something significant happens\u2014this can signal trap triggers or phase shifts.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps, amulet-based targeting rules  \n- Environment: Illusions, falling debris  \n- Systems: Rune alarms, reactive wall-hum indicators  \n- Faction Interaction: Guards bypass traps via amulets; players may not",
