      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no direct evidence that Thalia is compromised, but something may be off\u2014she\u2019s been involved in tense situations and was even attacked by Stafl, which raises uncertainty.\n\nBased on the projection, Thalia has limited direct detail, so trust is not clearly established either way. However, a few OBSERVED signals matter:\n\n- Caelynn the Half-Elf Sorcerer is coordinating with Thalia (e.g., \u201cTalking with Thalia about the plans\u201d and instructing her to deliver a potion), which suggests baseline trust from a party member.\n- Stafl \u201cAttacks Thalia after being revived,\u201d which implies either suspicion, confusion, or hidden factors affecting behavior in that moment.\n- The broader context includes corruption (e.g., guards with \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d), meaning paranoia is justified in this meeting.\n\nNo CANON or OBSERVED facts explicitly confirm Thalia is compromised, but the environment is unstable and at least one ally reacted violently toward her.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Relationships: Trusted by Caelynn (coordination and tasking)\n- Risk Indicators: Target of sudden aggression by Stafl\n- Context: Meeting occurs amid widespread corruption and paranoia in the city\n\nConclusion: Proceed cautiously\u2014no proof she\u2019s untrustworthy, but enough irregularity to warrant scrutiny.",
