      "answer": "TL;DR: Inaction accelerates the crisis\u2014each unresolved debate pushes the city closer to disaster, while threats (cult activity, tainted meat, and coordinated attacks) continue to spread unchecked.\n\nIf the council stalls, the biggest immediate risk is escalation without coordination. The city is already \u201cBrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d (OBSERVED, the city). That means delays directly worsen outcomes, not just postpone them.\n\nMeanwhile, multiple threats keep moving:\n- The tainted meat issue remains unresolved at the governance level (OBSERVED, the city), risking wider contamination.\n- \u201cCoordinated attacks occur across the city\u201d (CANON, the city geography), so delay gives enemies time to act in multiple locations.\n- The cult already threatens the city\u2019s stability (OBSERVED, the city operational_status).\n- A \u201cPlanned magical lockdown\u201d and sealing tunnels could isolate districts (OBSERVED), turning delay into fragmentation and panic.\n\nSocial pressure also builds: protests over the toll and unrest (CANON atmosphere) can destabilize order if leadership appears indecisive.\n\nThe players themselves are \u201cdelayed by lengthy deliberation\u201d (OBSERVED), meaning your most capable responders are effectively benched.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Governance: Council deadlock on tainted meat response\n- Operational Status: Brought closer to disaster; cult threat; planned lockdown\n- Geography: Hidden passages enable coordinated attacks\n- Atmosphere: Civil unrest and protests over tolls\n- Defenses: Risk of isolation if tunnels/access points are sealed",
