      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room is tense and chaotic\u2014marked by illusionary confusion, corrupted guards, and the Wolf\u2019s **decapitated; head removed from body**, with unsettling signs of deeper corruption still present.\n\nAfter the fight, the chamber feels unsettled rather than resolved. The most immediate visual is the Wolf: **decapitated; head removed from body**, his corpse a clear but disturbing centerpiece. If the players look closely, his defining corruption remains visible\u2014**an oily sheen to his eyes**, reinforcing the cult influence.\n\nAround the room, guards are still present, many **visibly tense** and some showing that same **oily sheen to their eyes**, suggesting the threat isn\u2019t over. Their formation\u2014**a ring along the wall**\u2014may still be partially intact but loosened by the chaos of the fight.\n\nThe space itself shows signs of magical disorientation: the aftermath of **illusory duplicates** and confusion lingers in how people move and react, with uncertainty about what was real. There may also be subtle environmental cues (like shifts in the chamber\u2019s hum) hinting that something deeper\u2014possibly the **secret escape tunnel beneath the council chamber**\u2014is still in play.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps may still be active (CANON, Players)\n- Enemies: Corrupted guards with oily eyes (OBSERVED, Guards)\n- Atmosphere: Tense, unstable, distrustful\n- Notable Feature: Wolf\u2019s **decapitated; head removed from body** and lingering corruption signs",
