      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events; after, he is **decapitated; head removed from body**, shifting from a cunning infiltrator to a defeated, revealing piece of evidence.\n\nBefore the council fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **second-in-command** guard and **cultist** working to **sabotage council decision-making**.\n- He actively **deceives the council**, using Persuasion/Deception to mislead and downplay the cult threat.\n- In combat, he relies on **illusory duplicates** and confusion tactics.\n- Operationally, he is evasive: **turns invisible**, attempts escape via **secret tunnels**, and coordinates with guards.\n- Mentally, he shows cracks: **desperate, begging for release or death, regretful**, suggesting internal conflict beneath the manipulation.\n\nAfter the council fight (OBSERVED):\n- His status is terminal: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n- No longer an active agent\u2014his role shifts from **manipulator to proof** of the cult\u2019s reach.\n- The noted **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** reinforces visible corruption, now examinable rather than hidden.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur \u2192 dead evidence\n- Rank: Second-in-command (before)\n- Tactics: Illusions, deception, invisibility (before)\n- Physical Condition: **Decapitated; head removed from body**, oily sheen eyes (after)\n- Alignment: Cult-affiliated betrayer of Mirathorn",
